cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "rsemverse: From RSEM Gene Results to Analysis-Ready Gene Tables"
authors:
  - family-names: Kumakura
    given-names: Daiki
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9859-0720"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24210460"
    description: "Archived release (Zenodo)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DaikiKumakura/rsemverse"
url: "https://daikikumakura.github.io/software/rsemverse.html"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An R package that turns RSEM *.genes.results files into analysis-ready gene tables for human and mouse bulk RNA-seq. It reads the files into a gene symbol by sample table of expected counts or TPM, then filters genes (edgeR filterByExpr rule, detection thresholds, most variable genes), keeps or removes built-in gene groups from the OrgDb, normalizes between samples (CPM, TMM, upper quartile, DESeq2 median of ratios, quantile), transforms values (log2, z-score, ranks) and returns a long table with the sample information.
keywords:
  - "RNA-seq"
  - "RSEM"
  - "gene symbol"
  - "R package"
